  "note": "Triennial election of the Limavady Urban District Council, 15 May 1939; no nominations were received, so the retiring councillors were deemed re-elected (Belfast News-Letter, 4 May 1939, p. 12). No nominations were received for the nine seats. The paper names the eight retiring councillors deemed re-elected and adds that the vacancy caused by the death of M. M. M'Causland in January 1938 still existed. No party label was printed. The Belfast Telegraph and Londonderry Sentinel of the same date carry the same list. Deemed re-elected (no nomination)."
